Chapter: JuliaKernel
  cites Gpu chapter DeviceEffect
  cites Gpu chapter DeviceMath

 An animated Julia set, as a [Device] compute kernel. One GPU thread per pixel
 takes its position as the initial z, iterates z = z*z + c for a shared c that
 orbits a circle with time, and colours by the escape count. The iteration is a
 tail-recursive helper with float state -> the plug lowers it to a WGSL loop,
 and the math is real f32 (smooth, unlike the fixed-point Mandelbrot).

 real-sin / real-cos come from Gpu chapter DeviceMath (correct bodies, replaced
 with hardware ops by the plug); real-from-int is the compiler builtin.

 We say:

Section: Parameters

  jl-width : Integer = 1024
  jl-half-w : Integer = 512
  jl-half-h : Integer = 384
  jl-max : Integer = 128

  jl-mod : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  jl-mod (x) (m) = x - (x / m) * m

Section: Iteration

 z = z*z + c until |z|^2 > 4 or the step cap; returns the escape count.

  jl-iter : Real, Real, Real, Real, Integer -> Integer
  jl-iter (zr) (zi) (cr) (ci) (n) =
    if n >= jl-max then jl-max
    else if zr * zr + zi * zi > 4.0 then n
    else jl-iter (zr * zr - zi * zi + cr) (2.0 * zr * zi + ci) cr ci (n + 1)

Section: Colour

  jl-chan : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  jl-chan (it) (mul) (phase) = jl-mod (it * mul + phase) 256

  jl-color : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  jl-color (it) (frame) =
    if it >= jl-max then 0
    else let f = frame
    in let r = jl-chan it 8 (30 + f)
    in let g = jl-chan it 5 (90 + f)
    in let b = jl-chan it 11 (160 + f)
    in r * 65536 + g * 256 + b

Section: Render

  jl-render : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  jl-render (gid) (frame) =
    let px = gid - (gid / jl-width) * jl-width
    in let py = gid / jl-width
    in let zr = real-from-int (px - jl-half-w) / 320.0
    in let zi = real-from-int (py - jl-half-h) / 320.0
    in let a = real-from-int frame / 40.0
    in let cr = 0.7885 * real-cos a
    in let ci = 0.7885 * real-sin a
    in jl-color (jl-iter zr zi cr ci 0) frame

Section: Julia Kernel

  julia-step : Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Device] Integer
  julia-step (outb) (frame) (gid) = act
    device-store outb gid (jl-render gid frame)
  end
